description:
Source: CI wall-time analysis of 2026-09-27; Noah confirmed the institute's 20 self-hosted runners are idle; parent epic.

Every HiSim job runs on GitHub-hosted runners (`runs-on: ubuntu-latest`), which on the organisation's Free plan means 20 concurrent jobs shared with every other repository of FZJ-IEK3-VSA. Listing the self-hosted runners needs org admin (`gh api orgs/FZJ-IEK3-VSA/actions/runners` answers 403 for a member), so before any workflow can target them somebody with that right has to write down:

- the labels they carry (`self-hosted`, `linux`, and whatever custom label the fleet has), the runner group, and which repositories it is allowed for;
- cores and RAM per machine, and whether Docker is installed and usable by the runner user (every HiSim job runs in the `ghcr.io/fzj-iek3-vsa/hisim-test:py311` container, which needs Docker on a self-hosted runner);
- whether the machines share a filesystem or a cache directory (an `actions/cache` alternative for the inputs cache), and whether outbound access to ghcr.io and the UTSP is open.

Put the answer into this issue and into `.github/ci-monitoring.md`. The sibling issue moves the heavy jobs over once this is known.
